{"schema_version":1,"merge_readiness":"advisory","lenses":[{"name":"correctness","score":8,"ran":true,"findings":[{"file":"tests/unit/adr-migration-claims-test.sh","category":"logic","severity":"low","line":128,"message":"SPEC-4's entire body is wrapped in `if [[ -f \"$_rl_guard\" ]]; then ... fi` with no `else` clause, so if `review-lens/plugin.sh` is absent the assertion silently produces no output (neither pass nor fail), while every other new SPEC (2, 3, 5, 6) fires `assert_fail` for a missing file because `grep -q ... 2>/dev/null` returns non-zero.","introduced":true},{"file":"tests/unit/adr-migration-claims-test.sh","category":"logic","severity":"low","line":10,"message":"The file-level header comment still reads \"`review-lens` still calls bare `extract_first_json_object`\" (lines 10-11), which directly contradicts SPEC-4's new assertion that no non-comment code line uses `extract_first_json_object`; the issue required this comment to be updated but the change left it stale.","introduced":false},{"file":"tests/unit/adr-migration-claims-test.sh","category":"logic","severity":"low","line":88,"message":"The SPEC-3 block comment still says \"review-lens is the counter-example… It is allowed to stay on `extract_first_json_object`\" (lines 88-89), but post-migration SPEC-3 always takes the migrated branch (line 106); the comment now describes a branch the test can never reach under normal conditions, creating misleading documentation about the test's actual control flow.","introduced":false}]},{"name":"performance","score":10,"ran":true,"findings":[]},{"name":"red-team","score":9,"ran":true,"findings":[{"file":"tests/unit/adr-migration-claims-test.sh","category":"coverage","severity":"low","line":113,"message":"SPEC-1 regex matches only markdown-bold `**not**` — a stale claim written with plain-text 'not migrated' (no asterisks) escapes the guard; introduced by this change.","introduced":true},{"file":"tests/unit/adr-migration-claims-test.sh","category":"logic","severity":"low","line":128,"message":"SPEC-4 wraps its body in `if [[ -f \"$_rl_guard\" ]]` with no else branch, so if plugin.sh is deleted the block emits no assertion and silently passes; mitigated by SPEC-2 which does fail loudly on absence.","introduced":true}]},{"name":"scope","score":10,"ran":true,"findings":[]},{"name":"security","score":10,"ran":true,"findings":[]},{"name":"sre","score":9,"ran":true,"findings":[{"file":"tests/unit/adr-migration-claims-test.sh","category":"coverage","severity":"low","line":129,"message":"SPEC-4's outer `if [[ -f \"$_rl_guard\" ]]; then … fi` has no else branch: if plugin.sh is absent or renamed the entire assertion silently produces no output (neither pass nor fail), so a file-deletion regression would go undetected; by contrast, the new SPEC-2 and SPEC-3 blocks correctly surface file-absence as assert_fail via the grep's non-zero exit code.","introduced":true}]}],"findings":[{"file":"tests/unit/adr-migration-claims-test.sh","category":"coverage","line":113,"severity":"low","lenses":["red-team"],"messages":["SPEC-1 regex matches only markdown-bold `**not**` — a stale claim written with plain-text 'not migrated' (no asterisks) escapes the guard; introduced by this change."]},{"file":"tests/unit/adr-migration-claims-test.sh","category":"coverage","line":129,"severity":"low","lenses":["sre"],"messages":["SPEC-4's outer `if [[ -f \"$_rl_guard\" ]]; then … fi` has no else branch: if plugin.sh is absent or renamed the entire assertion silently produces no output (neither pass nor fail), so a file-deletion regression would go undetected; by contrast, the new SPEC-2 and SPEC-3 blocks correctly surface file-absence as assert_fail via the grep's non-zero exit code."]},{"file":"tests/unit/adr-migration-claims-test.sh","category":"logic","line":128,"severity":"low","lenses":["correctness","red-team"],"messages":["SPEC-4 wraps its body in `if [[ -f \"$_rl_guard\" ]]` with no else branch, so if plugin.sh is deleted the block emits no assertion and silently passes; mitigated by SPEC-2 which does fail loudly on absence.","SPEC-4's entire body is wrapped in `if [[ -f \"$_rl_guard\" ]]; then ... fi` with no `else` clause, so if `review-lens/plugin.sh` is absent the assertion silently produces no output (neither pass nor fail), while every other new SPEC (2, 3, 5, 6) fires `assert_fail` for a missing file because `grep -q ... 2>/dev/null` returns non-zero."]}],"pre_existing":[{"file":"tests/unit/adr-migration-claims-test.sh","category":"logic","line":10,"severity":"low","lenses":["correctness"],"messages":["The file-level header comment still reads \"`review-lens` still calls bare `extract_first_json_object`\" (lines 10-11), which directly contradicts SPEC-4's new assertion that no non-comment code line uses `extract_first_json_object`; the issue required this comment to be updated but the change left it stale."]},{"file":"tests/unit/adr-migration-claims-test.sh","category":"logic","line":88,"severity":"low","lenses":["correctness"],"messages":["The SPEC-3 block comment still says \"review-lens is the counter-example… It is allowed to stay on `extract_first_json_object`\" (lines 88-89), but post-migration SPEC-3 always takes the migrated branch (line 106); the comment now describes a branch the test can never reach under normal conditions, creating misleading documentation about the test's actual control flow."]}],"summary":"3 merge-readiness finding(s) across 6 lens(es) (0 critical, 0 high).","escalation_note":null}
